From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the bezel a nib gives a text field

The theme swizzles -[NSTextField initWithFrame:] and -initWithCoder: to
make unbezeled the default, on the grounds that labels are the common
case. For a field made in code that is a default; for one loaded from a
nib it overrides what the nib says. Every input field in a nib therefore
draws flat, and - without the bezel's inset - with its text about two
points above its label.

Leave nib-loaded fields as the nib has them, and keep the unbezeled
default for fields made in code.
---
diff --git a/NSTextFieldCell+Eau.m b/NSTextFieldCell+Eau.m
index 0b66cd1..1e37ee1 100644
--- a/NSTextFieldCell+Eau.m
+++ b/NSTextFieldCell+Eau.m
@@ -262,12 +262,12 @@ titleRect.size.height += 2;
 
 - (id)initEauWithCoder:(NSCoder *)aDecoder
 {
-  self = [self initEauWithCoder:aDecoder];
-  if (self != nil)
-    {
-      [self setBezeled: NO];
-    }
-  return self;
+  /* A field from a nib already says whether it is bezeled -- an input
+     field in Interface Builder is -- so leave it as the nib has it.  The
+     unbezeled default is for fields made in code, where a label is the
+     common case; overriding the nib turned every input field in it into
+     a flat one, with its text drawn higher than its label. */
+  return [self initEauWithCoder:aDecoder];
 }
 
 @end
